   "description": "Comfort is the bringing of genuine relief to the person in pain — not the minimising of their suffering but the provision of strength, companionship, and hope that makes the suffering bearable. The Hebrew nacham and the Greek paraklēsis cover both the consoling and the encouraging: comfort is what the Comforter does, and the Comforter is the Spirit. God is the Father of all comfort. Comfort is always relational: it requires the presence of someone who sees the pain and responds to it with something that actually helps.",
